#################################################################
# FDD 17 — Educator Cred - Temporary Credentials
#
# Source: eight separate .docx, one per permit type, all under
# abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/17 - Educator Cred -
# Temporary Credentials/. Two companion diagram files in that folder
# ("Approvals All Types (omit SSW).vsdx", "MORE_flows_Permits.vsdx")
# and a PDF ("Career_Authorization_UI_flow.pdf") were skipped per
# fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's instruction to skip .vsdx/.pptx/etc.
# unless independently confirmed load-bearing — nothing in the eight
# .docx names them as a resolving reference for an otherwise-open
# question, so they were left unopened.
#
# Depth calibration (per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's "don't hold every
# FDD to the same depth" guidance — all eight documents share the same
# template/flow shape, so a full pass on all eight would mostly
# re-transcribe the same structure eight times):
#
# FULL DEPTH (docx comments + embedded wireframes actually viewed):
#   - Daily Substitute Permit — the simplest permit, AND the only one of
#     the eight .docx that carries a formal numbered "Addendum" section
#     (Feature 17.1 or 17.2 user stories with acceptance criteria) —
#     the other seven are narrative-plus-high-level-scenarios-table only,
#     with no equivalent formal numbering. 6 embedded images viewed
#     (decision flowchart + 5 real MiEdWorkforce UI screens: nav menu,
#     Employment Management landing, Roster of Employees, educator
#     profile "Apply for Certificate", Credentials/Permits tab with
#     "Apply for Permit" dropdown). 1 review comment (Sinha, 2026-03-18:
#     confirms Person/ID search is a valid alternate entry point —
#     folded into Req_17_1_1's notes, not a separate Annotation).
#   - School Administrator Permit — the "not renewable" edge case, and
#     structurally the most distinct of the eight (hire-date capture,
#     multiple district attestations under MCL 380.1246, a bachelor's-
#     degree hard stop, and its own mentor-assignment hard stop). 5
#     embedded images viewed, all real legacy MiEdWorkforce/MOECS UI:
#     educator search, and three named error-message screens (answers
#     incomplete / no bachelor's degree / no mentor assigned) plus the
#     submit/advisory screen. 2 review comments, both trivial ("Review",
#     "Confirming if this needs to be changed" — no resolution text
#     attached to either) — not modeled as Annotations, noted here only.
#   - Full Year Basic Substitute Permit — the richest of the three Full
#     Year variants (MCL-waiver branch, core/non-core endorsement
#     branch, 20-semester-hour minor fallback) and the one whose renewal
#     rule (IDP per-renewal-tier detail) is already modeled in
#     credentialing-domain.ttl as cred:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals, making
#     it the best candidate for confirming that rule against its source.
#     1 embedded image — turned out to be the SAME decision flowchart as
#     Daily Substitute Permit's image1.png (labeled "Daily Substitute
#     Permit (Display Statement #1)"), reused/mislabeled in this docx
#     rather than a Full-Year-Basic-specific flowchart. Not a modeling
#     gap — flagged here as a documentation-quality observation only;
#     not re-copied into wireframes/ a second time since it's a byte-
#     for-byte duplicate of wireframe-1.
#
# LIGHTER PASS (one Requirement per document, numbers/logic checked
# against cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits and related rules;
# no docx comment-thread or wireframe extraction — Extended Daily and
# Emergency Extended Daily do carry 2 wireframes each per the folder's
# .docx but they were not unpacked/viewed at this depth):
#   - Extended Daily Substitute Permit
#   - Emergency Extended Daily Substitute Permit
#   - Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit
#   - Renewals (the cross-permit renewal-rules reference doc)
#   - School Social Worker Permit
#
# requirementId scheme: Daily Substitute Permit's own "17.1.x"/"17.2.x"
# numbering is used verbatim where it exists. The other seven documents
# have no native numbering scheme of their own (no Addendum, and the
# High Level Scenarios table's "Ref" column only cross-references
# numbered paragraphs in that document's own prose, not a stable
# external identifier) — for those, this file mints "17.<ABBREV>.<n>"
# (e.g. "17.SA.1" for School Administrator) in FDD-source paragraph
# order, flagged here as an invented-not-native numbering scheme.
#
# =================================================================
# HEADLINE FINDING — cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits verified
# against its own source FDDs
# =================================================================
# Every single number in the rule's statement was independently
# confirmed against these eight FDDs and NONE were found to be wrong:
#   - Daily Substitute: 90 calendar days/assignment — Daily Sub FDD body
#     and 17.1.6 ("The Daily permit may be used ... for up to 90
#     calendar days").
#   - Extended Daily: +90 days, requires mentor + observation — Extended
#     Daily FDD's own application questions ask "Has the individual been
#     assigned a mentor...?" AND "Have they been observed with
#     satisfactory feedback?", both hard stops.
#   - Emergency Extended Daily: +90 days, 270-day total cap — both the
#     Extended Daily and Emergency Extended Daily FDDs state verbatim:
#     "the total allowable coverage in a single teaching assignment
#     could total 270 consecutive CALENDAR days."
#   - Full Year Basic: max 3 renewals / 4 years total — Daily Sub FDD
#     17.1.9 and the Renewals FDD, both verbatim "maximum of three
#     renewals... maximum of four years."
#   - Full Year Shortage: max 3 renewals, requires effective/highly
#     effective ratings — Renewals FDD verbatim: "Effective or highly
#     effective ratings are required within the assigned area for up to
#     three renewals."
#   - School Administrator: not renewable — Daily Sub FDD 17.1.8 and the
#     Renewals FDD's own "will not be able to be renewed" list, both
#     confirmed.
#   - School Social Worker: max 1 renewal — School Social Worker FDD
#     ("There is one renewal available for this permit") and the
#     Renewals FDD ("max renewal of 1"), both confirmed.
# NO NUMERIC OR LOGIC DISCREPANCY was found on any of the above — this
# is a genuine, fully corroborated confirmation, not a gap.
#
# What WAS found, that is a genuine gap: an entire EIGHTH permit type —
# "Full Year Expert" (a.k.a. "Expert Substitute Permit") — is named in
# the eligible-permit list of ALL EIGHT FDDs and has its own detailed
# renewal rule in the Renewals FDD (unlimited renewals, subject to IDP +
# mandatory mentor assignment + a bachelor's-degree-or-license fallback
# check for non-core assignments) but does not appear ANYWHERE in
# cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, in cred:CredentialCategory's
# enumerated list, or anywhere else in credentialing-domain.ttl. See
# cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below.
#
# Two smaller, real gaps also surfaced (both below as Annotations):
# no domain anywhere models "effective/highly effective" educator
# performance ratings (needed to gate Full Year Shortage renewals per
# the rule's own text), and the FDDs' "Needs Responses" flag — already
# flagged as a gap in miedw-v2/credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's
# Req_11_4_1 — recurs here as load-bearing logic in all eight documents
# (every one gates its confirmation message and worklist routing on a
# PPR-status × Needs-Responses combination), strengthening rather than
# duplicating that earlier finding.
#################################################################

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix staff: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

