#################################################################
# Requirements — Daily Substitute Permit (full depth; native 17.1.x/
# 17.2.x numbering from the FDD's own Addendum section)
#################################################################

cred:Req_17_1_0 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.0" ;
    sd:title "Submit Daily Substitute Permit application (end-to-end narrative flow)" ;
    sd:statement "The FDD's main 'Business Specifications' narrative (distinct from the numbered Addendum below) describes the full org-submitted permit application flow: Unique-ID search with PPR-flag gating, permit-type selection, academic-year confirmation, the valid-teaching-certificate and 60-semester-hour/2.0-GPA eligibility questions, attestation/digital signature, and a confirmation message that varies by (application status x Needs Responses flag) combination." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "See body text — condensed into Req_17_1_1 through Req_17_1_5's individual acceptance criteria below; this Requirement exists so the narrative section (as opposed to the Addendum's discrete user stories) is itself accounted for once, not left implicitly uncovered." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication, cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance, cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria ;
    sd:notes "Strong direct match: cred:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication's own whatWhenWho already says 'district/ISD/staffing-agency user submits... educators never self-submit a permit application' and its actor is explicitly 'District/ISD/Staffing Agency User' — this FDD is exactly that flow. See Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below for the one real gap found in this flow (the FDD's Pending PPR/Conviction Review/Pending Evaluation/Pending Payment/Approved status-and-Needs-Responses-flag vocabulary does not map cleanly onto cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration, and 'Needs Responses' itself is not a modeled field anywhere)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Search for an educator by Unique ID to initiate a temporary credential application" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD user, I want to Search for an educator by Unique ID, so that I can easily initiate a temporary credential application for the correct individual." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Requires appropriate profile permissions. Navigate Dashboard > Roster of Employees. Clicking the Name hyperlink opens the educator's profile. Navigate to the Credentials tab; see options to apply for Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approval. System displays Apply or Cancel." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, cred:Perm_PermitIssue ;
    sd:notes "Wireframes 2-6 (all confirmed by viewing) are direct visual confirmation of this exact navigation path (nav menu > Employment Management > Roster of Employees > educator profile > Credentials/Permits tab > Apply for Permit). Comment (Sinha, 2026-03-18, unresolved/no reply on record): 'A district can also use the Person/ID search to initiate a temporary credential' — a second entry point (direct Person/ID search rather than Roster of Employees) not otherwise described in the FDD body text; not modeled as a separate Requirement since it's an alternate path to the same Op_AdminIssuePermit call, but worth surfacing since it implies at least one other search UI (Personnel Search, per wireframe-2's own nav) feeds the same flow." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Block application initiation for an individual with an adverse PPR status" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD user, I want to be prevented from applying for an individual with an adverse PPR status, so that I am prevented from initiating an application for an individual who is currently ineligible due to adverse actions." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "If the Unique ID has a PPR flag indicating an actionable offense, display: 'Adverse actions have been taken on a credential for this individual...' when the user clicks Apply for Permit/Career Authorization/Special Education Approval. If the PPR flag is allowable/eligible (e.g. non-actionable misdemeanor), allow the user to proceed." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance ;
    sd:notes "Direct match on the Blocked/Clear-or-ConditionalClearance branching already modeled in Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance and dramatized identically in cred:Seq_SubmitPermitApplication's own sequence diagram (PPR status = Blocked > error; Clear/ConditionalClearance/Hold > proceed). No gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Show the full list of eligible permits for an individual" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD user, I want to see the full list of eligible permits for an individual upon selecting 'Apply for Permit', so that I can choose the correct temporary credential type quickly." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "System references the individual's existing temporary credentials and the user's district/ISD to display only available/eligible permit types from the full list: Daily Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Basic Substitute, Full-Year Shortage Substitute, Extended Daily or Emergency Extended Daily Substitute, School Administrator, School Social Worker." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit ;
    sd:notes "'Full Year Expert' appears in this eligible-permit list — same as in all seven other FDD 17 documents — and is the permit type this file's headline finding concerns (see cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below): no GET /permit-types-style filtering logic anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl/credentialing-domain.ttl accounts for it specifically, since the aggregate that would define it (CredentialDefinitionAggregate/CredentialCategory) never lists it at all." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.4" ;
    sd:title "Require digital signature attestation before submission" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD user, I want to be required to digitally sign the application, so that I can legally attest to the requirements and validity of the information provided." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Confirmation page prior to final submission, displaying an Advisory statement of legal considerations/district responsibilities; explicit checkboxes to agree to the Advisory and the permit's requirements; a dedicated free-form-text digital-signature area (the user's own name); submission blocked until both checkboxes and the signature are complete." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration ;
    sd:notes "Partial match: cred:Rule_CertificateDocumentGeneration models certificate PDF generation, not the attestation-capture step itself. Same gap already identified in credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_1_3 for the general (non-permit-specific) attestation flow — this FDD's version is simpler (checkboxes + free-text name, no separate typed-name field distinct from the checkboxes) but is the same underlying, still-unresolved attestation-modeling gap, not a new one. Wireframe-11 (School Administrator Permit's Submit Application screen, confirmed by viewing) shows the identical pattern." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.5" ;
    sd:title "Block duplicate endorsement/grade combination submissions" ;
    sd:statement "I want the system to block duplicate endorsement/grade so that policy limits are enforced." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "If the same endorsement/grade combination already exists (active), block submission and display an error message." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no invariant on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate enforces uniqueness of (endorsement, grade level) per individual/district/academic year for permits specifically — Extended/Emergency Extended Daily's own FDD describes the identical rule in much more detail ('The system will prevent a user from applying... for the same Endorsement and Grade Level combination, when there is an existing active Extended Daily Substitute Permit...'). Genuine coverage gap, corroborated across two of the eight FDDs." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.6" ;
    sd:title "Select Extended Daily/Emergency Extended Daily and see the 270-day total-coverage reminder" ;
    sd:statement "As a School District/ISD/Staffing Agency User, I want to select the Extended Daily or Emergency Extended Daily Substitute permit type, so that I can apply for coverage for a teaching assignment lasting more than 90 consecutive calendar days." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Extended Daily is offered only if an existing Daily Substitute Permit exists for the same individual/district/academic year; Emergency Extended is offered only if an existing Extended Daily Substitute Permit exists likewise. System reminds the user the combined Daily + Extended + Emergency Extended coverage 'could total 270 consecutive calendar days.'" ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:notes "Direct, exact numeric match — see this file's header for the full cross-check. No discrepancy." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.7" ;
    sd:title "Provide a renewal pathway for renewable permit types" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want to be able to renew Full Year Basic Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Shortage Substitute, and School Social Worker permits." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Clear renewal pathway for each of the four listed permit types; attestation + digital signature required prior to submission; messaging/confirmation throughout the renewal process." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Seq_RenewCredential, cred:Op_SubmitRenewal ;
    sd:notes "Genuine discrepancy worth flagging: cred:Seq_RenewCredential's own actor is 'Educator' (self-service, 'Who: Authenticated educator with renewable credential') and cred:Op_SubmitRenewal's gating permission cred:Perm_ApplicationSubmit is scoped scope:SelfOnly ('All authenticated educators'). But this FDD, and every other FDD-17 document, consistently describes PERMIT renewals (as opposed to certificate renewals) as org-submitted by a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user on the educator's behalf — the same actor as the original permit application (cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, gated by district/ISD-scoped cred:Perm_PermitIssue), not the educator. No org-submitted 'renew a permit on behalf of an educator' ApiOperation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl — Op_SubmitRenewal is the only renewal endpoint, and its actor/scope doesn't match what these FDDs describe. This corroborates the same Question_WorklistAssignmentScope-adjacent actor confusion already flagged in credentialing-domain.ttl, but specifically for renewals, which hadn't been checked before. See cred:Question_PermitRenewalActorMismatch below." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.8" ;
    sd:title "Prevent renewal applications for non-renewable permit types" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want the system to prevent renewal applications for Daily Substitute, Extended Daily Substitute, Emergency Extended Daily Substitute, and School Administrator permits, so that I avoid submitting applications for non-renewable credentials." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The option to apply for renewal is explicitly not available for these four permit types." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:notes "Direct match for the School Administrator (not-renewable) case; Daily/Extended/Emergency Extended are implicitly non-renewable in the rule's statement (no renewal count given, only duration caps) but the rule's text never says 'not renewable' for those three the way it explicitly does for School Administrator — a minor textual-completeness gap in the rule statement itself (not a numeric error), worth a light note rather than a full Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_1_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.1.9" ;
    sd:title "Enforce maximum renewal counts per renewable permit type" ;
    sd:statement "As a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user, I want to be able to have a max number of renewals for Full Year Basic Substitute, Full Year Expert, Full Year Shortage Substitute, and School Social Worker permits, so that renewals aren't over utilized." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Full Year Basic Substitute: max 3 renewals (4 years total). Full Year Shortage Substitute: max 3 renewals. School Social Worker: max 1 renewal. Full Year Expert: unlimited renewals, provided specific criteria are met." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:notes "The Full Year Basic / Full Year Shortage / School Social Worker numbers are an exact match — see this file's header cross-check. 'Full Year Expert Substitute Permits have unlimited renewals available, provided specific criteria are met' is the clearest single-sentence confirmation, across all eight FDDs, that Full Year Expert is a real, distinct, currently-unmodeled permit type — see cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Req_17_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.2" ;
    sd:title "Temporary Credentials User Feedback (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "All underlying logic for sending, tracking, and displaying emails, alerts and notifications are derived from Business Specification #6 (Alerts, Emails & Communications). This feature is strictly limited to the configuration of these tools (defining what is sent) specifically for the Educator Credentialing module. Additionally, Business Specification #4 (Business Rules Management) will specify when and to whom it is sent." ;
    sd:notes "Covers 17.2.1-17.2.7 (confirmation message content, Application Reference Number display, Conviction Review / Pending Payment messaging, and the two educator-facing PPR-completion and payment-link emails) — all seven stories are specific instances of the same (application status x Needs Responses flag) confirmation-message pattern already covered narratively by Req_17_1_0/Req_17_SA_7 below, with the actual send/track mechanism explicitly deferred to Communications by the FDD's own text, same pattern as credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_6/Req_16_3." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Email/communication behavior is explicitly owned by Business Specification #6 (Communications), matching the identical deferral already modeled for Req_11_6/Req_16_3 in credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_2 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — School Administrator Permit (full depth; no native
# numbering — 17.SA.<n> minted in source paragraph order)
#################################################################

cred:Req_17_SA_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.1" ;
    sd:title "Search for an educator and gate on PPR flag (School Administrator Permit)" ;
    sd:statement "Dependent upon profile permissions, the user searches for a Unique ID; a PPR flag on the individual blocks the application with an error message (this document's own text: 'Error message will be defined')." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "PPR flag on: error message displayed (text explicitly left TBD in this FDD, unlike Daily Substitute Permit's fully-specified equivalent message). PPR flag off: proceed to Apply for a permit (new/renewal)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_ProfessionalPracticeClearance ;
    sd:notes "Logic matches Req_17_1_2's Daily-Substitute equivalent exactly; the only difference is this FDD leaves its own error-message text as an explicit placeholder ('Error message will be defined') rather than a gap in the graph — noted here for traceability, not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is a documented, self-acknowledged TBD in the source, not a silent omission." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.2" ;
    sd:title "Display School Administrator Permit eligibility information (MCL 380.1246)" ;
    sd:statement "After permit-type selection, the system displays detailed eligibility information for the School Administrator Permit, referencing MCL 380.1246 and its subrules, and lists the categories of individuals who may be eligible." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Permit valid from date of payment through August 31 of the applied academic year (MCL 380.1246). Eligible-individual categories displayed: MI-certified admins needing renewal-credit time, out-of-state initial certification applicants, interim placements, MCL 380.1246(3)/(2) initial-certification seekers." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:notes "CredentialDefinitionAggregate's CredentialDefinitionRequirementRule DomainEntity is the right general shape for this ('Business rules defining eligibility criteria') but none of the MCL-380.1246-specific eligibility text is captured anywhere as actual data — same class of gap as most eligibility-criteria detail across this domain; not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is the same already-acknowledged general pattern (business rules are configuration data, not hand-authored graph content) rather than a School-Administrator-specific surprise." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.3" ;
    sd:title "Confirm academic year and capture hire date for School Administrator Permit" ;
    sd:statement "The system confirms the current academic year with the user, then prompts for the individual's hire date via a date picker." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Academic year populated from system date (July 1 rollover rule, same as every other permit type). Hire date required via date picker before proceeding to attestations." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate ;
    sd:notes "cred:ApplicantResponses ('Answers to business rule management questions') is the closest existing field but has no explicit hireDate concept called out — folded into the general ApplicantResponses shape rather than treated as a distinct gap, since that value object is deliberately opaque/schema-free by design." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.4" ;
    sd:title "Require multiple district attestations before proceeding (School Administrator Permit)" ;
    sd:statement "The system requires the district to attest to several statements (certified-administrator unavailability, the assignment being under 6 months for most eligible-individual categories, MCL 380.1246(3) individuals' 6-month/3.5-year enrollment-and-completion timeline, and audit/state-aid-deduction acknowledgment) before the application can proceed." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "If the district does not attest to one or more required statements, display an error and block progress (per wireframe-8, confirmed by viewing: 'All questions must be answered to qualify for School Administrator Permit')." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate ;
    sd:notes "Wireframe-8 (confirmed by viewing) is direct visual confirmation this is a real, implemented hard stop. The specific attestation content (6-month/3.5-year MCL 380.1246(3) timeline, state-aid-deduction audit acknowledgment) is not itself captured as structured data anywhere — same general 'eligibility criteria are configuration, not hand-authored graph content' pattern as Req_17_SA_2, not modeled as a separate Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.5" ;
    sd:title "Hard-stop on missing bachelor's degree (School Administrator Permit)" ;
    sd:statement "The system asks whether the individual holds a bachelor's or higher degree from a regionally/nationally accredited institution; answering No blocks the application." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "No -> error message, application cannot proceed (wireframe-9, confirmed by viewing: 'does not meet the Bachelor's Degree requirement for this permit'). Yes -> proceed to the mentor-assignment question." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:notes "Same pattern as Req_17_SA_2/4 — the eligibility CHECK exists conceptually (CredentialDefinitionRequirementRule) but the specific degree-requirement criterion is not captured as structured data. No separate Annotation; consistent with how eligibility-criteria detail is handled domain-wide." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.6" ;
    sd:title "Hard-stop on missing mentor assignment (School Administrator Permit)" ;
    sd:statement "For MCL 380.1246(3) individuals, the system asks whether the district did or will assign a mentor; answering No blocks the application. Answering Yes requires entering the mentor's name via a dynamically-filtered search (falling back to free text if no match)." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "No -> error (wireframe-10, confirmed by viewing: 'does not meet the permit requirement to have an assigned mentor'). Yes -> dynamically-filtered search field for certified educators, required, with a free-form fallback if the search returns no results." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits ;
    sd:notes "Strong, direct corroboration — cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits already explicitly lists SAP (School Administrator Permit) among the four permit types requiring mentor capture (EDSP, EEDSP, SAP, SSWP), and already models both the Mentor-Unique-ID (Staffing-validated) path and the free-form/external-mentor manual-review path. Wireframe-10 (confirmed by viewing) is direct visual proof this hard stop is real, implemented behavior, not merely a documented intention. No gap — this is exactly the kind of independent-FDD corroboration this review exercise exists to produce." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.7" ;
    sd:title "Submit School Administrator Permit application and display status-specific confirmation" ;
    sd:statement "Upon Submit, the system displays a confirmation message that varies by (application status x Needs Responses flag), and routes the application: Pending PPR (hold, awaiting PPR responses), Conviction Review (hold, PPR worklist), Pending Evaluation (submitted, assigned to OEE worklist), Pending Payment (hold, awaiting payment), Approved (issued)." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Five named invalid status/Needs-Responses combinations are explicitly rejected (Pending Evaluation+Y, Pending Payment+Y, Approved+Y, Pending PPR+N, Conviction Review+Y). Wireframe-11 (confirmed by viewing) shows the shared advisory/attestation/signature screen immediately preceding this step." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria, cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering ;
    sd:notes "See cred:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below (shared with Req_17_1_0) — this FDD's 'Pending Evaluation' status (routed to the OEE worklist) is the clearest of all eight documents that the FDDs' own status vocabulary is richer/differently-shaped than cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration (Draft/Submitted/PendingPayment/PendingDocuments/ProfessionalPracticeHold/RequiresManualReview/Approved/Denied/Cancelled/Blocked has no obvious 1:1 'Pending Evaluation' or 'Conviction Review' counterpart, and 'Needs Responses' is not a modeled field at all)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

cred:Req_17_SA_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SA.8" ;
    sd:title "School Administrator Permit is not renewable" ;
    sd:statement "This FDD does not describe any renewal pathway for the School Administrator Permit — consistent with both the Daily Substitute Permit FDD (17.1.8) and the Renewals FDD's own non-renewable list." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:notes "Triple-corroborated across three independent FDD documents (this one by omission, Daily Substitute Permit 17.1.8, and Renewals) — no discrepancy." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolAdminDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Full Year Basic Substitute Permit (full depth; no
# native numbering — 17.FYB.<n> minted in source paragraph order)
#################################################################

cred:Req_17_FYB_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.1" ;
    sd:title "Display Full Year Basic Substitute Permit eligibility information" ;
    sd:statement "After permit-type selection, the system displays Full Year Basic Substitute Permit eligibility text: a non-certified/endorsed individual may instruct students when a properly certified/endorsed teacher is unavailable; core-subject assignments require a matching transcript major or passing content-area MTTC scores; several MCL waiver provisions can waive one or more requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Eligibility text displayed; Back/Continue options; academic-year/expiration-date confirmation follows, same pattern as every other permit type." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation ;
    sd:notes "The core-subject major-or-MTTC logic matches Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's existing EndorsementDefinition.RequiredAssessments AND/OR model well. The four named MCL waiver provisions (380.1531f Tribal MOU, 380.1281(3) Foreign MOA/Residency/SPI waiver, 380.1233c Detroit Public Schools Community District, 380.505 University Faculty Public School Academy) are not captured as data anywhere — same 'eligibility criteria is configuration' pattern noted elsewhere in this file, not a separate Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYB_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.2" ;
    sd:title "MCL-waiver branch bypasses test-score/subject-area checks and forces Pending Evaluation" ;
    sd:statement "If the application is authorized under one of the four named MCL waiver provisions, the system shows a dropdown of waiver selections; each existing waiver selection skips test-score and subject-area confirmation entirely, and all such applications are set to Pending Evaluation status." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "MCL waiver selected -> skip standard eligibility checks, application status forced to Pending Evaluation, user still required to enter at least one endorsement and grade level." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: no invariant or business rule anywhere models an MCL-waiver override path that skips standard validation and forces a specific application status — this is a real, previously-invisible branch in the eligibility logic (distinct from the ordinary 60-semester-hour/GPA path modeled in Req_17_FYB_3) that Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria/Rule_ManualReviewTriggering don't account for. Genuine coverage gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYB_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.3" ;
    sd:title "60-semester-hour/associate-degree eligibility gate (non-waiver path)" ;
    sd:statement "If no MCL waiver applies, the system asks whether the individual has completed at least 60 semester hours of credit (grade C or better) or an associate degree from a CHEA/USED-recognized institution; No hard-stops the application." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "No -> error: 'The Full Year permit application cannot be submitted because the individual does not meet the credit requirements for the permit.' Yes -> proceed to endorsement/grade-level selection." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria ;
    sd:notes "Same eligibility-gate shape already used by Daily Substitute Permit's equivalent 60-hour/GPA question (Req_17_1_0) and Extended Daily's version — consistent pattern across permit types, no new gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYB_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.4" ;
    sd:title "Endorsement selection with core/non-core branching and 20-semester-hour minor fallback" ;
    sd:statement "The system requires at least one endorsement/grade-level selection; for core-subject endorsements without a verified passing MTTC score, it asks whether the educator holds at least a minor (20 semester credit hours) in the content area as a fallback path to Pending Evaluation status." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Non-core endorsement -> straight to application review. Core endorsement with verified score -> application review. Core endorsement, no verified score, 20-hour minor confirmed -> application review, status set to Pending Evaluation. Core endorsement, no verified score, no minor -> error: 'Educator is not eligible for this endorsement because there is no verification of test scores or a major for one or more of the subject areas.'" ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation ;
    sd:notes "The core/non-core branch and MTTC score check match Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation well. The specific '20 semester credit hour minor' fallback quantity is new, previously-uncaptured detail — not modeled as a separate Annotation since it is additive precision on an already-modeled rule rather than a structural gap, but worth folding into that rule's own statement in a future domain-file pass." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYB_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.5" ;
    sd:title "Submit Full Year Basic Substitute Permit application and display status-specific confirmation" ;
    sd:statement "Same (application status x Needs Responses flag) confirmation-message pattern as every other permit type: Pending PPR, Conviction Review, Pending Evaluation, Pending Payment, Approved, with the same five invalid combinations rejected." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria, cred:Rule_ManualReviewTriggering ;
    sd:notes "Same pattern already covered by Req_17_1_0/Req_17_SA_7 — see cred:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch below; not re-modeled as a separate Annotation, just cross-referenced." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYB_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYB.6" ;
    sd:title "Full Year Basic Substitute Permit renewal: max 3 renewals / 4 years, per-renewal IDP requirements" ;
    sd:statement "Full Year Basic Substitute Permit renewals are capped at 3 (4 years of teaching total), each renewal requiring an Individual Development Plan (IDP) — 1st renewal: enrollment in a state-approved teacher-prep program; 2nd and 3rd renewals: minimum 6 semester hours completed since the previous renewal." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, cred:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals ;
    sd:notes "Exact match on both the renewal count/duration (Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits) and the per-renewal-tier IDP detail (Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals — whose own statement already spells out the identical 1st/2nd/3rd-renewal tiers this FDD describes, sourced from the Renewals FDD). Strong corroboration, no discrepancy — this is the single cleanest confirmation in the whole FDD-17 set that a previously-modeled rule's fine detail is accurate against its actual source document." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — lighter-pass documents (one Requirement each; numbers/
# logic checked against cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits and
# related rules only)
#################################################################

cred:Req_17_ED a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.ED.1" ;
    sd:title "Extended Daily Substitute Permit: eligibility, mentor + observation gate, and duration" ;
    sd:statement "Extended Daily Substitute Permit is offered only when the individual already holds a Daily Substitute Permit for the same district/ISD/academic year, provides an additional 90 consecutive calendar days of coverage, and requires (in order): a >90-day-need confirmation, the same 60-semester-hour/GPA gate as other permit types, a mentor-assignment question (with dynamic-search-or-free-form mentor name capture), and an observed-with-satisfactory-feedback question — all four hard stops." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits ;
    sd:notes "Numbers match exactly (+90 days; see this file's header). Mentor requirement matches cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits (EDSP is already in its listed scope). The 'observed with satisfactory feedback' hard stop is NOT captured by that rule or anywhere else in credentialing-domain.ttl — a genuine coverage gap distinct from the mentor-capture requirement itself (mentor assignment and a documented satisfactory observation are two separate hard stops in this FDD, only the first is modeled)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17ExtendedDailyDoc .

cred:Req_17_EED a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.EED.1" ;
    sd:title "Emergency Extended Daily Substitute Permit: 270-day cap and Extended-vs-Emergency-Extended auto-determination" ;
    sd:statement "Emergency Extended Daily Substitute Permit provides a further 90 consecutive calendar days after Extended Daily (270-day total cap across Daily + Extended + Emergency Extended), granted at the discretion of the Superintendent of Public Instruction, not guaranteed, with processing up to 4 weeks. The system automatically determines whether a new application is 'Extended' or 'Emergency Extended' based on whether the endorsement/grade-level combination differs from or duplicates an existing Extended Daily Substitute Permit for the same district/individual/academic year." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits ;
    sd:notes "270-day cap and mentor/observation hard stops (shared with Extended Daily, same gate) match cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits/Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits (EEDSP is already in the latter's listed scope). The permit-type AUTO-DETERMINATION logic (differing/added grade+endorsement -> new Extended Daily; same grade+endorsement -> Emergency Extended) is business-rule detail not represented anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl — a real, previously-uncaptured piece of eligibility logic, though narrower in scope than the Extended Daily gap already flagged in Req_17_ED (that 'observed with satisfactory feedback' gap applies identically here, not repeated as a second Annotation)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17EmergencyExtendedDailyDoc .

cred:Req_17_FYS a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.FYS.1" ;
    sd:title "Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit: professional certificate + <=.5 FTE gate, and effective/highly-effective-rated renewals" ;
    sd:statement "Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit requires the educator to hold a Professional/Advanced Professional/Permanent/Life/Continuing certificate (Provisional does not qualify) and the assignment to be <=.5 FTE; renewals (max 3) require effective or highly effective performance ratings in the assigned area." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:notes "Max-3-renewals and effective/highly-effective-ratings requirement match cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits exactly — see this file's header. The professional-certificate-tier eligibility gate and the <=.5 FTE numeric-field validation are not captured anywhere as structured data (same 'eligibility criteria as configuration' pattern noted elsewhere). More significant: nothing in credentialing-domain.ttl, staffing-domain.ttl, or any other converted mied-v3 domain models educator PERFORMANCE RATINGS (effective/highly effective) at all — see cred:Question_EducatorPerformanceRatingSourceMissing below, this FDD's own source for that half of the rule." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearShortageDoc .

cred:Req_17_REN a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.REN.1" ;
    sd:title "Cross-permit renewal rules and eligibility factors" ;
    sd:statement "This document is the cross-permit reference for which temporary credentials can/cannot be renewed, their renewal caps, and the shared eligibility-factor list business rules draw on (non-MCL vs. MCL permit history, 4th-renewal same-endorsement/grade/district check, academic progress, mentor assignment, formal-observation ratings, remaining endorsement/grade-level coverage)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, cred:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals, cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits ;
    sd:notes "This is the primary source document for cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits and cred:Rule_IdpForPermitRenewals, and confirms both are accurate (see this file's header). It is also the single clearest source, across all eight FDDs, for the missing Full Year Expert permit type: 'Expert Substitute Permits will have unlimited renewals available when the following criteria is met: Development and implementation of an IDP; the district/school must assign and maintain a mentor teacher... If the assignment is in a non-core discipline area and the individual qualified for an initial full-year expert substitute permit under only subrule (1)(g)(i)... the applicant shall verify that the business or industry license or credential... is valid... or that the individual holds a bachelor's degree, or higher.' See cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing below." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17RenewalsDoc .

cred:Req_17_SSW a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "17.SSW.1" ;
    sd:title "School Social Worker Permit: LARA license eligibility, supervision requirement, and 1-renewal cap" ;
    sd:statement "School Social Worker Permit requires a Master of Social Work degree (or equivalent), a valid LARA-issued LLMSW or LMSW license (number + expiration date captured), enrollment/acceptance in an approved SSW preparation program, and supervision by a fully credentialed Michigan School Social Worker (captured the same way as a mentor — dynamic search or free-form, required, with supporting documentation retained for audit). Exactly one renewal is available, requiring demonstrated progress toward program completion." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits, cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits ;
    sd:notes "Max-1-renewal matches cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits exactly. The supervising-School-Social-Worker capture matches cred:Rule_MentorAssignmentRequirementForPermits's existing scope (SSWP is already listed, and that rule's own worked example is specifically an SSW-Permit-with-an-external-mentor scenario) — strong corroboration, no gap on the mentor/supervision side. The LARA license number + expiration date fields themselves are not captured anywhere in cred:ApplicantResponses or any other ValueObject — a minor, narrow coverage gap (a specific external-license-reference shape, not previously seen in any other permit type's FDD) not modeled as a separate Annotation given its narrow scope, but noted here for completeness." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17SchoolSocialWorkerDoc .

#################################################################
# Cross-cutting Annotations
#################################################################

cred:Question_FullYearExpertPermitTypeMissing a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "An eighth permit type, 'Full Year Expert' (a.k.a. 'Expert Substitute Permit'), is named in the eligible-permit list of ALL EIGHT FDD 17 documents (Daily Substitute Permit's own 17.1.3/17.1.7/17.1.9, and identically in Extended Daily, Emergency Extended Daily, Full Year Basic, Full Year Shortage, School Administrator, School Social Worker, and Renewals) alongside the seven permit types cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits already models. The Renewals FDD gives it real, specific renewal criteria: unlimited renewals subject to (1) an approved IDP, (2) mandatory district-assigned-and-maintained mentor teacher, and (3) for non-core-discipline assignments qualified only under a specific subrule, verification of a valid business/industry license or a bachelor's degree or higher at renewal time. None of this appears anywhere in cred:CredentialCategory's enumerated list, cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits's statement, or any other rule/aggregate in credentialing-domain.ttl. This is the single largest gap found in this review pass — a whole permit type with its own eligibility and renewal rules, entirely unmodeled, not merely under-specified." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_1_3, cred:Req_17_1_9, cred:Req_17_REN, cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17RenewalsDoc .

cred:Question_ApplicationStatusVocabularyMismatch a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "All eight FDD 17 documents gate their confirmation messaging and worklist routing on a (application status x Needs Responses flag) combination, using a status vocabulary — Pending PPR, Conviction Review, Pending Evaluation (routed to the OEE worklist), Pending Payment, Approved — that does not map cleanly 1:1 onto cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate's AppState_* enumeration (Draft/Submitted/PendingPayment/PendingDocuments/ProfessionalPracticeHold/RequiresManualReview/Approved/Denied/Cancelled/Blocked). 'Pending Evaluation' most plausibly corresponds to RequiresManualReview and 'Conviction Review' to ProfessionalPracticeHold, but neither mapping is stated anywhere, and the 'Needs Responses' boolean flag itself — which gates FIVE explicitly-named invalid status combinations in every one of the eight FDDs — is not a modeled field on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or any ValueObject at all. This is the same underlying gap credentialing-fdd-11-16.ttl's Req_11_4_1 already flagged from a different FDD (11.4.1's PPR-flag/Needs-Responses eligibility filter) — FDD 17 corroborates it as load-bearing, cross-permit-type logic rather than a one-off, strengthening rather than duplicating that earlier finding." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_1_0, cred:Req_17_SA_7, cred:Req_17_FYB_5, cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate ;
    sd:impact "H" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

cred:Question_PermitRenewalActorMismatch a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "discrepancy" ;
    rdfs:comment "cred:Seq_RenewCredential (credentialing-sequences.ttl) models renewal as educator self-service ('Who: Authenticated educator with renewable credential', actor 'Educator') and its gating cred:Op_SubmitRenewal is permissioned via cred:Perm_ApplicationSubmit, scoped scope:SelfOnly ('All authenticated educators'). Every FDD 17 document that discusses permit renewals (Daily Substitute Permit 17.1.7, and the Renewals FDD's own framing throughout) instead describes permit renewals as submitted by a School district/ISD/Staffing Agency user on the educator's behalf — the same org-submitted actor as the original permit application (cred:Op_AdminIssuePermit, gated by district/ISD-scoped cred:Perm_PermitIssue), consistent with both FDDs' shared assumption that 'Temporary Credentials are applied for by a district or ISD on behalf of an individual.' No org-submitted 'renew a permit' ApiOperation exists anywhere in credentialing-api.ttl. Seq_RenewCredential most plausibly describes CERTIFICATE renewal (matching FDD 11/16's scope) rather than PERMIT renewal — but nothing currently distinguishes the two paths in the graph, and permit renewal as these FDDs describe it may be entirely unimplemented." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_1_7, cred:Seq_RenewCredential, cred:Op_SubmitRenewal ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No invariant on cred:CredentialApplicationAggregate or cred:IssuedCredentialAggregate enforces uniqueness of an (endorsement, grade level) combination per individual/district/academic year for permit applications. Extended Daily/Emergency Extended Daily's own FDD describes the identical rule in much more operational detail (blocking a duplicate Extended Daily Substitute Permit application for the same endorsement+grade combination), corroborating this as real, cross-permit-type business logic rather than a one-off wish-list item from Daily Substitute Permit's FDD alone." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_1_5 ; sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17DailySubDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No business rule or invariant anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl models an MCL-waiver override path for Full Year Basic Substitute Permit applications: when one of the four named MCL waiver provisions (380.1531f Tribal MOU, 380.1281(3) Foreign MOA/Residency/SPI waiver, 380.1233c Detroit Public Schools Community District, 380.505 University Faculty Public School Academy) applies, this FDD says the system skips standard test-score/subject-area validation entirely and force-sets the application to Pending Evaluation status regardless of ordinary eligibility outcome. This is a distinct branch from the ordinary 60-semester-hour/GPA eligibility gate (Req_17_FYB_3, which IS covered by cred:Rule_AutoApprovalCriteria) and from the auto-approval/manual-review criteria generally — a real, previously-uncaptured override path." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_FYB_2 ; sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearBasicDoc .

cred:Question_EducatorPerformanceRatingSourceMissing a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits's own statement requires 'effective/highly effective ratings' for Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit renewals (confirmed verbatim against the Renewals FDD and the Full Year Shortage Substitute Permit FDD). No domain converted into mied-v3 so far (credentialing, staffing, or otherwise) models educator performance/effectiveness ratings as data anywhere — not as a ValueObject, not as an external-system dependency, not even as an open question elsewhere. This is a genuine, narrow but real gap: the rating data this specific renewal rule depends on has no known source in the solution design at all yet." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_17_FYS, cred:Rule_PermitDurationAndRenewalLimits ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd17FullYearShortageDoc .
